From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 08:28:44 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: pmp: Start CoreAnalytics on the J604 PMP

The T8132 PMP owner starts RTKit system endpoint 7 (CoreAnalytics) only
on boards for which apple_pmp_telemetry_retained_board() is true, which
is only the J713. The J604 PMP needs it too. On a J604 running an
earlier stub firmware than 25G83, the PMP advertised endpoint 7 next to
0-4 and 0x20 and did not acknowledge the IOP power state until the
endpoint was started and had its buffer: without it the probe stopped
with "IOP power acknowledgment failed: -62", and with it the firmware
logged "PMP started". The same behaviour on 25G83 is still to be
confirmed on hardware.

The J604's PMP is retained from the bootloader in the same way as the
J713's (its display vote bridge already reports "retained existing PMP
owner"), and the predicate has no user other than the endpoint 7
decision, so add the J604 to it and document what it means. RTKit
starts the endpoint and waits for its buffer only when the firmware
advertises it, so a firmware without endpoint 7 is unaffected. Nothing
changes on the J713.

The J604 PMP is described in the same way as the J713's in the 25G83
and 26B123 j604ap device trees: /arm-io/pmp, /arm-io/dart-pmp and
iop-pmp-nub differ only in phandles and in the board's lts-config and
lts-clpc-voltage calibration, which the loader copies from the running
device tree.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/soc/apple/pmp-telemetry.c | 10 ++++++++--
 drivers/soc/apple/pmp.rs          |  2 +-
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/apple/pmp-telemetry.c b/drivers/soc/apple/pmp-telemetry.c
index fb9c1605e8..61311fa650 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/apple/pmp-telemetry.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/pmp-telemetry.c
@@ -16,10 +16,16 @@
 #include <linux/soc/apple/pmp-temps.h>
 #include <linux/soc/apple/pmp-power-policy.h>
 
+/*
+ * T8132 boards whose PMP the owner retains from the bootloader. Their PMP
+ * firmware waits for RTKit system endpoint 7 (CoreAnalytics) before it
+ * acknowledges the IOP power state.
+ */
 bool apple_pmp_telemetry_retained_board(void)
 {
-	return of_machine_is_compatible("apple,j713") &&
-	       of_machine_is_compatible("apple,t8132");
+	return of_machine_is_compatible("apple,t8132") &&
+	       (of_machine_is_compatible("apple,j713") ||
+		of_machine_is_compatible("apple,j604"));
 }
 
 static LIST_HEAD(apple_pmp_telemetry_list);
diff --git a/drivers/soc/apple/pmp.rs b/drivers/soc/apple/pmp.rs
index 2e069a34f4..d33f55c259 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/apple/pmp.rs
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/pmp.rs
@@ -699,7 +699,7 @@ impl platform::Driver for PmpDriver {
                 &[(from_fourcc(b"BDID"), bdid), (from_fourcc(b"DVID"), dvid)],
             )?,
         };
-        // EP7 is a qualified startup dependency only on the retained J713 PMP.
+        // EP7 is a startup dependency of the retained J713 and J604 PMPs.
         // SAFETY: the predicate only reads machine compatibility.
         let needs_coreanalytics =
             cfg.coreanalytics && unsafe { bindings::apple_pmp_telemetry_retained_board() };
